 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Chef Viktor is at the hospital after being hit by a car. The doctor examines his leg, but Viktor makes up a story to protect the person who hit him.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "У вас надрыв связок.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "Это не очень страшно.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "Не нагружайте ногу.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "Спасибо.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "Какая причина вашей травмы?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "Я попал под машину.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "Будете заявлять в полицию?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "Нет.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "Я забыл поставить машину на ручник.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "И она на меня наехала.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "Понятно.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "Заявлять не буду.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Let's listen to their conversation.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "У вас надрыв связок.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'You have a partial ligament tear.' Here 'you' sets up the idea, while 'ligament' comes at the end for emphasis.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "Это не очень страшно.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'It's not too serious.' Notice the word order: 'this' comes first, and 'scary' finishes the sentence.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "Не нагружайте ногу.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Keep your weight off that leg.' Here 'load' sets up the idea, while 'foot' comes at the end for emphasis.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "Спасибо.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Thank you.' The key word here means 'thank you', which Chef Viktor combines with 'thank you'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "Какая причина вашей травмы?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'What is the cause of your injury?' There is no question word here — in Russian, rising intonation on 'injury' is enough to make it a question. Chef Viktor answers straight away.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "Я попал под машину.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I got hit by a car.' Chef Viktor starts with 'I' and pairs it with 'hit' to make the point clear.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "Будете заявлять в полицию?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Will you report to the police?' the speaker puts 'will be' up front so the listener immediately catches the tone, followed by 'declare'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "Нет.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'No.' Listen for the word meaning 'no' right alongside 'no' in this line.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "Я забыл поставить машину на ручник.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I forgot to put the car on handbrake.' The first content word means 'I', and 'handbrake' rounds out the thought.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "И она на меня наехала.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'And it ran over me.' A compact expression built around 'it' and 'confront'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "Понятно.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I see.' In Russian, 'clear' leads into 'clear' in a very natural everyday phrasing. And Chef Viktor jumps in.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "Заявлять не буду.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I will not report it.' The little negative word sits right in front of the verb for 'will be', just like 'not' in English. Now let's hear the whole thing once more.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "У вас надрыв связок.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
